[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174299] [:db/retract 17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174300] [:db/retract 17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174301] [:db/retract 17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174303] {:db/id 17592186176034 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" "question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" "question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" "question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175889 :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=0.5x+7.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=6$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.5x+7 \\\\  & =0.5(6)+7 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" "question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175888 :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(82,70).$ So, our actual value is $y=70.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=82$ has the $y$-coordinate $65.$ So, our estimated value is $\\widehat{y}=65.$\n\n![](images/99/99e3741f602802e636e2e49ef755954343079b8c0d98453dac9364ddc08ef16f.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =70-65 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176035 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" "question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" "question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175890 :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c7bf33ee8878c6dc8e33622a5abe79a068b483ed19c0e177ecea31ab34b8777.png)\n\n  \n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=4,$ the regression equation underestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=4$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual} >     \\textrm{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates  this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b02727029ed43c985da639287afa452cbe1985dc2bae8eaa4f16452ac4c01518.png)\n\n   \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/id #uuid "9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/math-academy-id "q-134719" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=-1.5x+2.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=12$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $-14?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =-1.5x+2 \\\\  & =-1.5(12)+2 \\\\  & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =-14-(-16) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" "answer-c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" "answer-8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" "answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" "answer-0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" :answer/id #uuid "2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" :answer/id #uuid "c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" :answer/id #uuid "8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer/id #uuid "a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29" :answer/id #uuid "0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176340 :question/problem "An antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $x$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=3.2x+4.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual $5$ decades after the artwork was produced if the actual value of the artwork after $5$ decades is $$23\\,000?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =3.2x+4.5 \\\\  & =3.2(5)+4.5 \\\\  & =20.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =23-20.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,500.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186174298 :answer-field/correct "answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer-field/choices ["answer-844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" "answer-66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" "answer-6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" "answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" :answer/id #uuid "844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$(-1\\,500)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" :answer/id #uuid "66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$(-2\\,500)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" :answer/id #uuid "6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$1\\,500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/id #uuid "640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$2\\,500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/id #uuid "f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-134737" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=0.75x+2.25.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=8$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $11.25?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.75x+2.25 \\\\  & =0.75(8)+2.25 \\\\  & =8.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =11.25-8.25 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/id #uuid "29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" "answer-fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" "answer-0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" "answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" "answer-5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" :answer/id #uuid "91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" :answer/id #uuid "fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" :answer/id #uuid "0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer/id #uuid "a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184" :answer/id #uuid "5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/id #uuid "66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/math-academy-id "q-134736" :question/problem "A veterinarian collects data on a puppy's height $y$ (in inches) at certain times $x$ (in months) since it was born. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=2.2x+3.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual after $5$ months if the actual height of the $5$-month old puppy is $15.5\\,in?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated height using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.2x+3.5 \\\\  & =2.2(5)+3.5 \\\\  & =14.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =15.5-14.5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $1\\,in.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/id #uuid "177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer-field/choices ["answer-860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" "answer-874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" "answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" "answer-aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" "answer-986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" :answer/id #uuid "860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.5\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" :answer/id #uuid "874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer/id #uuid "a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" :answer/id #uuid "aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f" :answer/id #uuid "986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,in" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/id #uuid "e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134753" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=1.8x+1.4.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=7$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =1.8x+1.4 \\\\  & =1.8(7)+1.4 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-14 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/id #uuid "790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer-field/choices ["answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" "answer-ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" "answer-03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" "answer-8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" "answer-428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer/id #uuid "452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" :answer/id #uuid "ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" :answer/id #uuid "03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" :answer/id #uuid "8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67" :answer/id #uuid "428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/id #uuid "855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-134788" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f940a05c937b3158ce737959dee4685d216e6d55d6651672aa910cdb2c492f1e.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,1).$ So, our actual value is $y=1.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $0.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=0.$\n\n![](images/93/937c0307a74881c87e6a33c47b32a1ac2d5124326b13538455640cd9fc88c14e.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" "answer-fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" "answer-27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" "answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" "answer-6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" :answer/id #uuid "a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" :answer/id #uuid "fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" :answer/id #uuid "27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer/id #uuid "e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c" :answer/id #uuid "6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/id #uuid "fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/math-academy-id "q-134797" :question/problem "![](images/81/815ba0a13bc8cbd7adcfadc63b80d6f2da36c9755166694915fa2f297be27721.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $x$ years after its release to the market. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,12).$ So, our actual value is $y=12.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $10.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=10.$\n\n![](images/ab/ab5e194ac03482b1cee6bdb7aa35e323b40a1ad63769e60acbb000adb7aa1e82.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,000.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" "answer-5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" "answer-e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" "answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" "answer-eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/id #uuid "a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$1\\,000$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/id #uuid "5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$1\\,200$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/id #uuid "e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$1\\,500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/id #uuid "d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$2\\,000$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/id #uuid "eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$2\\,500$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176343 :question/problem "![](images/27/278c910d3ce96e613e04cb1b849e57775064c49de45972358c07bfa90d882c8b.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=2,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=2$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}>\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates (*not* overestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The plot shows that the residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the residuals are close to $0$ and are randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, we can conclude that our regression line is probably a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186174316 :answer-field/correct 17592186174317 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/id #uuid "e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/math-academy-id "q-134830" :question/problem "![](images/31/31a72edb688af9be0481fc98346aa5655190e32564ddc003eb7bdd1c83d41ee1.png)\n\nAn economist records data on the volume of corn exports $y$ (in thousands of tons) from the United States to a particular country, $x$ number of years since $2010.$\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=6,$ the regression equation underestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=6$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates (*not* underestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The plot shows that the residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the residuals are close to $0$ and are randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, we can conclude that our regression line is probably a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/id #uuid "134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" "answer-054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" "answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" "answer-352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" "answer-ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" :answer/id #uuid "73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" :answer/id #uuid "054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer/id #uuid "2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" :answer/id #uuid "352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b" :answer/id #uuid "ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/id #uuid "21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-134825" :question/problem "![](images/57/57ba7828008f3e3c271ae4c1b6d444005f40c09bf6ba99e614f3b6414c1e56c2.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $t$ years after its release to the market. The residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=6,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=6$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as time increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/fe/fe18ccc94d0cc98f971b6482d4e31c7ec7066b5cec427108ddd8d1e6609e08ba.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/id #uuid "68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" "answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" "answer-61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" "answer-cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" "answer-f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" :answer/id #uuid "e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer/id #uuid "655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" :answer/id #uuid "61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" :answer/id #uuid "cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff" :answer/id #uuid "f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/id #uuid "1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/math-academy-id "q-134824" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae6bc049d3bf3bbdf1a609b6cda4c3b4e9cc1699b387099d265e048a32be68d6.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=2,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=2$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}>\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates (*not* overestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f5f3a4dc75324a6ef415c987a62139e2dbd51c5b35a56d5a35f410781087c43.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" "answer-30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" "answer-f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" "answer-8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" "answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" :answer/id #uuid "a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" :answer/id #uuid "30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" :answer/id #uuid "f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" :answer/id #uuid "8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer/id #uuid "3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177047 :tutorial/content "Given a dataset of paired numerical observations $(x,y)$ and the corresponding linear regression model $\\widehat{y} =f(x),$ the **residual** for a particular observation $(x, y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-f(x) \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe subtract the *estimated* value predicted by the model from the actual *observed* value.\n\nTo illustrate this concept graphically, consider the following example.\n\nThe owner of an ice cream shop keeps track of the average daily temperature $x$ (measured in $^\\circ \\mathrm{F}$) and the resulting daily ice cream sales $y$ (in dollars). The scatter plot for several randomly selected days and the corresponding linear regression line are shown below. \n\n![](images/fc/fc149b8d911a7a9863df9cc25c635d6155accd676e83e335a65d9083596b779b.png)\n\nSuppose the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny= 2.5 x +165.\n$$\n\nLet's use our regression line to compute the residual of the point with coordinates $\\color{red}(82, 360)$ (shown in red on our graph). \n\nFirst, notice that since the highlighted data point has coordinates ${\\color{red}(82, 360)},$ our actual value is $y = {\\color{red}360}.$\n\nNext, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.5x+165 \\\\  & =2.5(82)+165 \\\\  & =370\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n![](images/38/3843c71b50251ae035378507ffb22cfade48dff8e1544d8e1317e4e6d611f7a1.png)\n\nFinally, we compute the residual: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =360-370 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nThe residual tells us that the linear model *overestimates* the true volume of ice cream sales by $\\[math]10$ when the outside temperature is $82^\\circ\\,\\textrm{F}.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177048 :tutorial/content "A **residual plot** displays the values of the independent variable along the horizontal axis and the residuals along the vertical axis. \n\nThe scatter plot below represents data from a four-day sample on the number of people visiting a swimming pool and the average daytime temperature, in degrees Celsius. The line $\\ell$ is the corresponding linear regression line. \n\n![](images/62/6228578012fac7e42bedeb7ab7ad5fc9f42432aed8d5751b675df560bc867417.png)\n\n    \n\nThese residuals for each of the four data points are highlighted below:\n\n![](images/d7/d70c44fe7b8fce43a8962ac104651acced75e10598e865a3b3c80d09f16ce234.png)\n\n    \n\nIf we calculate the numerical values for the residuals at each data point (from left to right), we get the following results:\n\n$$\n-4, \\quad 8, \\quad -8, \\quad 4\n$$\n\nTo compute our residual plot, we plot each $x$-value and its corresponding residual on some coordinate axes: \n\n![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177051 :tutorial/content "![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)\n\nWe should be aware of the following interpretations for residual plots:\n\n- Any point *above* the horizontal axis represents a *positive* residual. A positive residual means that the regression model *underestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\n- Any point *below* the horizontal axis represents a *negative* residual. A negative residual means that the regression model *overestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\nResidual plots can also be used to assess whether a trend line is a \"good\" fit for the corresponding data:\n\n- If a linear trend line is a good fit for the data, the residuals should be scattered randomly above and below the horizontal axis and be relatively close to zero.\n\n- In cases where the residuals show some clear pattern, this usually indicates that the data has no linear trend.\n\nThe residuals are scattered randomly about the horizontal axis in our last example. However, they are not close to zero, indicating that the trend line is a weak fit for the data." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176138 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186175889 :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=0.5x+7.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=6$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12?$"] [17592186175889 :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.5x+7 \\\\  & =0.5(6)+7 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186175888 :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(82,70).$ So, our actual value is $y=70.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=82$ has the $y$-coordinate $65.$ So, our estimated value is $\\widehat{y}=65.$\n\n![](images/99/99e3741f602802e636e2e49ef755954343079b8c0d98453dac9364ddc08ef16f.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =70-65 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $5.$"] [17592186175890 :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c7bf33ee8878c6dc8e33622a5abe79a068b483ed19c0e177ecea31ab34b8777.png)\n\n  \n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=4,$ the regression equation underestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."] [17592186175890 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=4$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual} >     \\textrm{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates  this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b02727029ed43c985da639287afa452cbe1985dc2bae8eaa4f16452ac4c01518.png)\n\n   \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] ["question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/id #uuid "9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93"] ["question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/math-academy-id "q-134719"] ["question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=-1.5x+2.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=12$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $-14?$"] ["question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =-1.5x+2 \\\\  & =-1.5(12)+2 \\\\  & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =-14-(-16) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3"] ["answer-2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" :answer/id #uuid "2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6"] ["answer-2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" :answer/id #uuid "c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e"] ["answer-c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" :answer/id #uuid "8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d"] ["answer-8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer/id #uuid "a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add"] ["answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29" :answer/id #uuid "0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29"] ["answer-0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/correct "answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add"] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-2b24c861-005d-5443-874f-c3222611aae6"] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-c2705e8b-ac1b-58f1-ae18-4b2bb36c099e"] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-8468c7dc-8ac8-581c-b848-951838cc7b9d"] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-a101f9ee-8feb-534f-9b74-3c43f81b6add"] ["answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-0690fc09-2812-5def-a5c0-242e3c651d29"] ["question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-76ab6950-70a8-5dae-93a2-6d63d16060f3"] [17592186176034 :knowledge-point/questions "question-9d55db4e-8bf0-577f-a32c-7bdda150fe93"] [17592186176340 :question/problem "An antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $x$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=3.2x+4.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual $5$ decades after the artwork was produced if the actual value of the artwork after $5$ decades is $$23\\,000?$"] [17592186176340 :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =3.2x+4.5 \\\\  & =3.2(5)+4.5 \\\\  & =20.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =23-20.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,500.$"] [17592186176340 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" :answer/id #uuid "844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a"] ["answer-844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" :answer/value "$$(-1\\,500)$"] ["answer-66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" :answer/id #uuid "66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2"] ["answer-66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" :answer/value "$$(-2\\,500)$"] ["answer-6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" :answer/id #uuid "6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e"] ["answer-6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" :answer/value "$$1\\,500$"] ["answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/id #uuid "640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82"] ["answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/value "$$2\\,500$"] [17592186174298 :answer-field/correct "answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82"] [17592186174298 :answer-field/choices "answer-844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a"] [17592186174298 :answer-field/choices "answer-66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2"] [17592186174298 :answer-field/choices "answer-6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e"] [17592186174298 :answer-field/choices "answer-640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82"] ["question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/id #uuid "f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55"] ["question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-134737"] ["question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=0.75x+2.25.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=8$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $11.25?$"] ["question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =0.75x+2.25 \\\\  & =0.75(8)+2.25 \\\\  & =8.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =11.25-8.25 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/id #uuid "29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1"] ["answer-91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" :answer/id #uuid "91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb"] ["answer-91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" :answer/id #uuid "fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575"] ["answer-fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575" :answer/value "-2.75"] ["answer-0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" :answer/id #uuid "0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46"] ["answer-0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46" :answer/value "2.5"] ["answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer/id #uuid "a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc"] ["answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184" :answer/id #uuid "5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184"] ["answer-5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184" :answer/value "3.5"] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/correct "answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc"] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/choices "answer-91fe5890-b2fc-5848-beaf-a30d780e51eb"] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/choices "answer-fc739e9c-e7c6-5a19-823f-c35c9f284575"] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/choices "answer-0d78fe95-a05e-5eb4-b5c6-d25059010a46"] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/choices "answer-a1810fff-2ec2-5b6f-b1e9-1a2f8c7a4adc"] ["answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1" :answer-field/choices "answer-5f544aa2-e646-591f-8a84-14be73528184"] ["question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-29475db4-a660-51b2-8f9a-a2d8b85e63b1"] [17592186176034 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f64a4538-a38b-5427-b753-a3e4f5424a55"] ["question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/id #uuid "66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098"] ["question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/math-academy-id "q-134736"] ["question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/problem "A veterinarian collects data on a puppy's height $y$ (in inches) at certain times $x$ (in months) since it was born. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=2.2x+3.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual after $5$ months if the actual height of the $5$-month old puppy is $15.5\\,in?$"] ["question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated height using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.2x+3.5 \\\\  & =2.2(5)+3.5 \\\\  & =14.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =15.5-14.5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $1\\,in.$"] ["question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/id #uuid "177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622"] ["answer-860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" :answer/id #uuid "860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240"] ["answer-860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240" :answer/value "-1.5\\,in"] ["answer-874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" :answer/id #uuid "874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90"] ["answer-874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90" :answer/value "-1\\,in"] ["answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer/id #uuid "a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09"] ["answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09" :answer/value "1\\,in"] ["answer-aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" :answer/id #uuid "aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c"] ["answer-aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c" :answer/value "2.5\\,in"] ["answer-986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f" :answer/id #uuid "986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f"] ["answer-986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f" :answer/value "2\\,in"] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/correct "answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09"] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/choices "answer-860cc4ac-4d0f-5373-9938-2c6e8931d240"] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/choices "answer-874e5c1d-7313-523e-b2bd-2d3c8fa83a90"] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/choices "answer-a8513cdf-2331-554c-8660-9e7e500c6f09"] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/choices "answer-aae6a24f-103b-534b-852d-7d2b3995e87c"] ["answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622" :answer-field/choices "answer-986a6fb3-cec8-5e57-9bf2-aab9895fd98f"] ["question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-177b610f-1786-5112-9662-337212616622"] [17592186176034 :knowledge-point/questions "question-66a5e8a2-f155-513a-b41f-dffb1f1fb098"] ["question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/id #uuid "e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8"] ["question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134753"] ["question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=1.8x+1.4.\n$$\n\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=7$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12?$"] ["question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =1.8x+1.4 \\\\  & =1.8(7)+1.4 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-14 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/id #uuid "790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47"] ["answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer/id #uuid "452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857"] ["answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" :answer/id #uuid "ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756"] ["answer-ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756" :answer/value "-2.5"] ["answer-03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" :answer/id #uuid "03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98"] ["answer-03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98" :answer/value "1.5"] ["answer-8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" :answer/id #uuid "8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7"] ["answer-8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7" :answer/value "2.6"] ["answer-428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67" :answer/id #uuid "428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67"] ["answer-428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/correct "answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857"] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/choices "answer-452ae623-e358-52d4-bb76-b1a2bfd57857"] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/choices "answer-ae9ad99f-0561-5517-bfcc-0e3a33f16756"] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/choices "answer-03780f09-8ea3-5a8a-96e2-a084196fcb98"] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/choices "answer-8d2a5595-366e-5bca-b60a-4192671812d7"] ["answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47" :answer-field/choices "answer-428d4fab-d069-5a00-988d-33cdfa0aae67"] ["question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-790fc10f-cefb-5f65-a677-549fa2e80b47"] [17592186176034 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e8526d11-e962-5974-8b9d-23623deb26c8"] ["question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/id #uuid "855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd"] ["question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-134788"] ["question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f940a05c937b3158ce737959dee4685d216e6d55d6651672aa910cdb2c492f1e.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?"] ["question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,1).$ So, our actual value is $y=1.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $0.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=0.$\n\n![](images/93/937c0307a74881c87e6a33c47b32a1ac2d5124326b13538455640cd9fc88c14e.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6"] ["answer-a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" :answer/id #uuid "a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869"] ["answer-a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" :answer/id #uuid "fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df"] ["answer-fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" :answer/id #uuid "27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da"] ["answer-27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da" :answer/value "0.5"] ["answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer/id #uuid "e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35"] ["answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c" :answer/id #uuid "6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c"] ["answer-6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c" :answer/value "1.5"] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/correct "answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35"] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-a1c198d5-43fb-50f1-82b6-00fe92910869"] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-fb1533e7-cc35-5e5f-8c0a-d26f3f69e1df"] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-27cb4f4c-cab2-57f5-8d0f-1d5d3acbd3da"] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-e9ec9563-a8af-54a5-8104-e5811d0f0b35"] ["answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-6bd2fbc5-af88-5e57-848a-2616a89a8b6c"] ["question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-98f4db4e-2c19-5da3-9efd-62ed734fe2e6"] [17592186176033 :knowledge-point/questions "question-855a07b7-e3c5-5f4d-b62e-d65fbbb7b6dd"] ["question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/id #uuid "fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400"] ["question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/math-academy-id "q-134797"] ["question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/problem "![](images/81/815ba0a13bc8cbd7adcfadc63b80d6f2da36c9755166694915fa2f297be27721.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $x$ years after its release to the market. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?"] ["question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,12).$ So, our actual value is $y=12.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $10.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=10.$\n\n![](images/ab/ab5e194ac03482b1cee6bdb7aa35e323b40a1ad63769e60acbb000adb7aa1e82.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,000.$"] ["question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1"] ["answer-a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/id #uuid "a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35"] ["answer-a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/value "$$1\\,000$"] ["answer-5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/id #uuid "5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823"] ["answer-5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/value "$$1\\,200$"] ["answer-e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/id #uuid "e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b"] ["answer-e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/value "$$1\\,500$"] ["answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/id #uuid "d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498"] ["answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/value "$$2\\,000$"] ["answer-eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/id #uuid "eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14"] ["answer-eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/value "$$2\\,500$"] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/correct "answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498"] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/choices "answer-a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35"] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/choices "answer-5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823"] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/choices "answer-e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b"] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/choices "answer-d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498"] ["answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/choices "answer-eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14"] ["question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1"] [17592186176033 :knowledge-point/questions "question-fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400"] [17592186176343 :question/problem "![](images/27/278c910d3ce96e613e04cb1b849e57775064c49de45972358c07bfa90d882c8b.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=2,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."] [17592186176343 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=2$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}>\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates (*not* overestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The plot shows that the residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the residuals are close to $0$ and are randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, we can conclude that our regression line is probably a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] [17592186176343 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186174316 :answer-field/correct 17592186174317] ["question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/id #uuid "e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f"] ["question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/math-academy-id "q-134830"] ["question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/problem "![](images/31/31a72edb688af9be0481fc98346aa5655190e32564ddc003eb7bdd1c83d41ee1.png)\n\nAn economist records data on the volume of corn exports $y$ (in thousands of tons) from the United States to a particular country, $x$ number of years since $2010.$\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=6,$ the regression equation underestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."] ["question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=6$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates (*not* underestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The plot shows that the residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the residuals are close to $0$ and are randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, we can conclude that our regression line is probably a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] ["question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/id #uuid "134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975"] ["answer-73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" :answer/id #uuid "73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c"] ["answer-73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" :answer/id #uuid "054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732"] ["answer-054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer/id #uuid "2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073"] ["answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" :answer/id #uuid "352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2"] ["answer-352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b" :answer/id #uuid "ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b"] ["answer-ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/correct "answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073"] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/choices "answer-73f7d3b7-91e6-570a-bd65-c26c0642358c"] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/choices "answer-054a56f6-55ec-52ce-ab62-9c1453929732"] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/choices "answer-2ef6bc27-3115-58a1-b77f-67255e130073"] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/choices "answer-352e01c3-879d-5727-bf6b-3280d64091f2"] ["answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975" :answer-field/choices "answer-ce5b51ac-6dba-5bfc-a317-89116956d03b"] ["question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-134720c3-c104-501b-a6e2-c5acd7dfa975"] [17592186176035 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e996d8e3-bba2-534b-9d62-28bb3781b36f"] ["question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/id #uuid "21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae"] ["question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-134825"] ["question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/problem "![](images/57/57ba7828008f3e3c271ae4c1b6d444005f40c09bf6ba99e614f3b6414c1e56c2.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $t$ years after its release to the market. The residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $t=6,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."] ["question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $t=6$ is negative. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}<\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model overestimates this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as time increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/fe/fe18ccc94d0cc98f971b6482d4e31c7ec7066b5cec427108ddd8d1e6609e08ba.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] ["question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/id #uuid "68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af"] ["answer-e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" :answer/id #uuid "e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d"] ["answer-e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer/id #uuid "655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803"] ["answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" :answer/id #uuid "61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d"] ["answer-61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" :answer/id #uuid "cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe"] ["answer-cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff" :answer/id #uuid "f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff"] ["answer-f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/correct "answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803"] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/choices "answer-e37e0b0d-edbe-572b-bbae-c0a6f093dd5d"] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/choices "answer-655fdb32-13f3-5d7e-9b25-717fb4f2e803"] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/choices "answer-61171849-b617-5513-94ec-86c38a67041d"] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/choices "answer-cb6be770-2cbe-5612-874c-85394d3d6abe"] ["answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af" :answer-field/choices "answer-f2e5c06d-3710-503b-87f7-8b6b650645ff"] ["question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-68c8672b-b047-56da-be89-fb76699846af"] [17592186176035 :knowledge-point/questions "question-21d8d0de-cc80-527b-ade5-cff77e1f75ae"] ["question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/id #uuid "1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199"] ["question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/math-academy-id "q-134824"] ["question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae6bc049d3bf3bbdf1a609b6cda4c3b4e9cc1699b387099d265e048a32be68d6.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y).$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. When $x=2,$ the regression equation overestimates the value of $y.$\n\nII. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n\nIII. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."] ["question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=2$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual}>\\text{Estimated},$ and therefore the model underestimates (*not* overestimates) this data point.\n\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/2f/2f5f3a4dc75324a6ef415c987a62139e2dbd51c5b35a56d5a35f410781087c43.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""] ["question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3"] ["answer-a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" :answer/id #uuid "a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3"] ["answer-a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" :answer/id #uuid "30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3"] ["answer-30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3" :answer/value "I, II, and III"] ["answer-f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" :answer/id #uuid "f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d"] ["answer-f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" :answer/id #uuid "8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f"] ["answer-8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer/id #uuid "3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb"] ["answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb" :answer/value "None"] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/correct "answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb"] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-a8a52756-8d54-5488-b516-f0f46632e8a3"] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-30cc2096-72bf-53ab-80cd-0e53283f4fe3"] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-f1372349-8b30-54f1-9a67-58ef6c5b2f3d"] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-8422f803-42bc-5dbd-9a9b-5c17b0bab74f"] ["answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3" :answer-field/choices "answer-3c13437d-0881-5fe4-8a20-2ee35a2c1ddb"] ["question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0a67e86b-e489-54d7-865b-2fc901ce36f3"] [17592186176035 :knowledge-point/questions "question-1f3c0f66-15fe-5ce9-aae2-49226c3a0199"] [17592186177047 :tutorial/content "Given a dataset of paired numerical observations $(x,y)$ and the corresponding linear regression model $\\widehat{y} =f(x),$ the **residual** for a particular observation $(x, y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-f(x) \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe subtract the *estimated* value predicted by the model from the actual *observed* value.\n\nTo illustrate this concept graphically, consider the following example.\n\nThe owner of an ice cream shop keeps track of the average daily temperature $x$ (measured in $^\\circ \\mathrm{F}$) and the resulting daily ice cream sales $y$ (in dollars). The scatter plot for several randomly selected days and the corresponding linear regression line are shown below. \n\n![](images/fc/fc149b8d911a7a9863df9cc25c635d6155accd676e83e335a65d9083596b779b.png)\n\nSuppose the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny= 2.5 x +165.\n$$\n\nLet's use our regression line to compute the residual of the point with coordinates $\\color{red}(82, 360)$ (shown in red on our graph). \n\nFirst, notice that since the highlighted data point has coordinates ${\\color{red}(82, 360)},$ our actual value is $y = {\\color{red}360}.$\n\nNext, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.5x+165 \\\\  & =2.5(82)+165 \\\\  & =370\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n![](images/38/3843c71b50251ae035378507ffb22cfade48dff8e1544d8e1317e4e6d611f7a1.png)\n\nFinally, we compute the residual: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =360-370 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nThe residual tells us that the linear model *overestimates* the true volume of ice cream sales by $\\[math]10$ when the outside temperature is $82^\\circ\\,\\textrm{F}.$"] [17592186177048 :tutorial/content "A **residual plot** displays the values of the independent variable along the horizontal axis and the residuals along the vertical axis. \n\nThe scatter plot below represents data from a four-day sample on the number of people visiting a swimming pool and the average daytime temperature, in degrees Celsius. The line $\\ell$ is the corresponding linear regression line. \n\n![](images/62/6228578012fac7e42bedeb7ab7ad5fc9f42432aed8d5751b675df560bc867417.png)\n\n    \n\nThese residuals for each of the four data points are highlighted below:\n\n![](images/d7/d70c44fe7b8fce43a8962ac104651acced75e10598e865a3b3c80d09f16ce234.png)\n\n    \n\nIf we calculate the numerical values for the residuals at each data point (from left to right), we get the following results:\n\n$$\n-4, \\quad 8, \\quad -8, \\quad 4\n$$\n\nTo compute our residual plot, we plot each $x$-value and its corresponding residual on some coordinate axes: \n\n![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)"] [17592186177051 :tutorial/content "![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)\n\nWe should be aware of the following interpretations for residual plots:\n\n- Any point *above* the horizontal axis represents a *positive* residual. A positive residual means that the regression model *underestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\n- Any point *below* the horizontal axis represents a *negative* residual. A negative residual means that the regression model *overestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\nResidual plots can also be used to assess whether a trend line is a \"good\" fit for the corresponding data:\n\n- If a linear trend line is a good fit for the data, the residuals should be scattered randomly above and below the horizontal axis and be relatively close to zero.\n\n- In cases where the residuals show some clear pattern, this usually indicates that the data has no linear trend.\n\nThe residuals are scattered randomly about the horizontal axis in our last example. However, they are not close to zero, indicating that the trend line is a weak fit for the data."] [17592186176138 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0]] "retractions" [[17592186175889 :question/problem "Consider the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is\n$y=0.5x+7$.\nAccording to the model, what is the residual at $x=6$ if the actual value of $y$ corresponding to this value of $x$ is $12$?"] [17592186175889 :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^(^) &= 0.5x + 7 \\\\\n&= 0.5(6) + 7 \\\\\n&= 10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - y^(^) \\\\\n&= 12 - 10 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186175888 :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}\n$$\n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(82,70)$. So, our actual value is $y=70$.\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=82$ has the $y$-coordinate $65$. So, our estimated value is\n\n$$\n\\widehat{y}=65\n$$\n\n![](images/99/99e3741f602802e636e2e49ef755954343079b8c0d98453dac9364ddc08ef16f.png)\n\nAs a result,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - y^(^) \\\\\n&= 70 - 65 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $5$."] [17592186175890 :question/problem "![](images/7c/7c7bf33ee8878c6dc8e33622a5abe79a068b483ed19c0e177ecea31ab34b8777.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x,y)$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. When $x=4$, the regression equation underestimates the value of $y$.\n2. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n3. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."] [17592186175890 :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The residual equals the actual value minus the estimated value:\n$\\textrm{Residual} = \\text{Actual} - \\textrm{Estimated}$\nFrom the plot, the residual at $x=4$ is positive. So, we have that $\\text{Actual} > \\textrm{Estimated}$, and therefore the model underestimates this data point.\n- Statement II is false. The plot shows the residuals tend to decrease as $x$ increases. So, there is a trend, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b0/b02727029ed43c985da639287afa452cbe1985dc2bae8eaa4f16452ac4c01518.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the residuals are *not* randomly scattered above and below the horizontal axis, our regression line is *not* a good fit for the given data.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] [17592186176340 :question/problem "An antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $x$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is\n$y = 3.2x + 4.5$.\nWhat is the residual $5$ decades after the artwork was produced if the actual value of the artwork after $5$ decades is $$23000$?"] [17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174299] [17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174300] [17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174301] [17592186174298 :answer-field/choices 17592186174303] [17592186176343 :question/problem "![](images/27/278c910d3ce96e613e04cb1b849e57775064c49de45972358c07bfa90d882c8b.png)\n\nThe residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on a set of bivariate numerical data $(x, y)$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. When $x = 2$, the regression equation overestimates the value of $y$.\n2. The residuals appear to be randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n3. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."] [17592186177047 :tutorial/content "Given a dataset of paired numerical observations $(x,y)$ and the corresponding linear regression model\n\n$$\n\\widehat{y} =f(x)\n$$\n\nthe **residual** for a particular observation $(x, y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - f(x) \\\\\n&= y - y^(^)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe subtract the *estimated* value predicted by the model from the actual *observed* value.\n\nTo illustrate this concept graphically, consider the following example.\n\nThe owner of an ice cream shop keeps track of the average daily temperature $x$ (measured in $^\\circ \\mathrm{F}$) and the resulting daily ice cream sales $y$ (in dollars). The scatter plot for several randomly selected days and the corresponding linear regression line are shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fc149b8d911a7a9863df9cc25c635d6155accd676e83e335a65d9083596b779b.png)\n\nSuppose the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny= 2.5 x +165\n$$\n\nLet's use our regression line to compute the residual of the point with coordinates $\\color{red}(82, 360)$ (shown in red on our graph).\n\nFirst, notice that since the highlighted data point has coordinates ${\\color{red}(82, 360)}$, our actual value is\n\n$$\ny = {\\color{red}360}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny^(^) &= 2.5x + 165 \\\\\n&= 2.5(82) + 165 \\\\\n&= 370\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/38/3843c71b50251ae035378507ffb22cfade48dff8e1544d8e1317e4e6d611f7a1.png)\n\nFinally, we compute the residual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nResidual &= Actual - Estimated \\\\\n&= y - y^(^) \\\\\n&= 360 - 370 \\\\\n&=-10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe residual tells us that the linear model *overestimates* the true volume of ice cream sales by $\\[math]10$ when the outside temperature is $82^\\circ\\,\\textrm{F}$."] [17592186177048 :tutorial/content "A **residual plot** displays the values of the independent variable along the horizontal axis and the residuals along the vertical axis.\n\nThe scatter plot below represents data from a four-day sample on the number of people visiting a swimming pool and the average daytime temperature, in degrees Celsius. The line $\\ell$ is the corresponding linear regression line.\n\n![](images/62/6228578012fac7e42bedeb7ab7ad5fc9f42432aed8d5751b675df560bc867417.png)\n\nThese residuals for each of the four data points are highlighted below:\n\n![](images/d7/d70c44fe7b8fce43a8962ac104651acced75e10598e865a3b3c80d09f16ce234.png)\n\nIf we calculate the numerical values for the residuals at each data point (from left to right), we get the following results:\n\n$$\n-4, \\quad 8, \\quad -8, \\quad 4\n$$\n\nTo compute our residual plot, we plot each $x$-value and its corresponding residual on some coordinate axes:\n\n![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)"] [17592186177051 :tutorial/content "![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)\n\nWe should be aware of the following interpretations for residual plots:\n\n- Any point *above* the horizontal axis represents a *positive* residual. A positive residual means that the regression model *underestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n- Any point *below* the horizontal axis represents a *negative* residual. A negative residual means that the regression model *overestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\nResidual plots can also be used to assess whether a trend line is a \"good\" fit for the corresponding data:\n\n- If a linear trend line is a good fit for the data, the residuals should be scattered randomly above and below the horizontal axis and be relatively close to zero.\n- In cases where the residuals show some clear pattern, this usually indicates that the data has no linear trend.\n\nThe residuals are scattered randomly about the horizontal axis in our last example. However, they are not close to zero, indicating that the trend line is a weak fit for the data."]]}]